ucers rankin bass  the stop-motion holiday animation  specialists  withdrew from the project leaving toho  to replace the ape with godzilla  ebro was also slated to appear and  destroy all monsters but  the big lobster was eventually dropped  from the script and the monster's brief  turn in 1969's all monsters attack  aka godzilla's revenge was simply  recycled footage from sea monster  ebero finally returned to the spotlight  in godzilla final wars  though its appearance was anything but  flattering with the creatures attack on  an oil refinery being thwarted by the  film's mutant soldiers  kamikoros was actually the name of three  stupendous praying mantises that menaced  both godzilla and his offspring minya in  the 1967 movie son of godzilla  the creatures impressive marionette  creations by the film special effects  director sadamasa arikawa  were first glimpsed as man-sized  mantises on a remote island before a  radioactive storm caused them to grow to  more than 50 meters in length  three king-sized kamakuras called  gymantis in the english language dub of  son of godzilla then tormented the newly  hatched minia before godzilla arrived to  fry two of them with his atomic breath  while the third was dispatched by the  island's other monstrous arthropod  inhabitant the spider kumonga  single and multiple marionette kamakuras  also appeared briefly in all monsters  attack and  1972's godzilla vs gaigan before a cgi  kamakuras turned up in godzilla final  wars  in this film the creature was seen to  possess the same camouflage abilities as  real-life fantasies not that it helped  kamakuras as the insect was quickly  sussed out by godzilla and  skewered on a transmission tower  kamikuros wasn't the only  insect bedeviling godzilla minia and the  human stars of son of godzilla  hidden inside a rocky valley was kumanga  a 150-foot spider with an appetite for  anything that crosses its path  once awakened kumonga ensnared minya and  akamakuras in its thick sticky web  which unlike most spiders jetted out  from its mouth  not its spinnerets and dispatched the  mantis with its creepy stabbing stinger  minia appeared next on the menu until  godzilla came to the rescue  the ensuing brawl was one of the film's  best displays of special effects  and undoubtedly one of its most  challenging  as the kumonga marionette required two  to three technicians to operate the  wires on each of its eight legs  eventually a combined blast of atomic  breath from father and son  brought down the spider but it or a  close relative was back in 1968 for  destroy all monsters  where it teamed with mothra to coat king  ghidorah in webbing during the films  concluding battle royale  kumanga's final screen appearance to  date was in godzilla final wars where it  displayed  a new talent a web that expanded from a  single strand to a net  this did little to stop godzilla who  simply grabbed hold of kumanga's web and  hurled him out of sight one of the  hardest working monsters in toho's  stable of kaiju  the burrowing flame ray breathing  dinosaur baragon has appeared in  numerous features  and television series over the past half  century though it's been  incognito for some of those turns  baragon made its debut in 1966 as  frankenstein vs baragon or  frankenstein conquers the world as it's  known in the states  the monster served as a replacement for  godzilla who was initially intended to  face off against toho's take on  frankenstein's monster  before production changes necessitated a  changeup baragon then returned to toho  from 1968's destroy all monsters though  its screen time was limited  why well according to some accounts it  was due to the monster's most  distinguishing feature  its long floppy ears the movie special  effects team was  concerned that this particular aspect of  the head design would make it difficult  to execute the monster's showcase  sequence  in which it tunneled under and destroyed  the arctic triumph in paris so  baragon was relegated to the background  while gorosaurus  a dinosaur from 1969's king kong escapes  got the big scene instead  in the ensuing decades baragon remained  a popular figure in countless  godzilla-related manga  novels and video games but it wouldn't  return to future work until 2001  when the creature helped to defend japan  against the rampaging godzilla in giant  monsters  all-out attack gabra is the nelson muntz  of touhou's roster of monsters  a mean-spirited bully with a distinctive  mocking laugh  and a penchant for pounding on smaller  creatures  are you alright man i  think so how about now  gabara is featured in just one film the  truly  eccentric all monsters attack aka  godzilla's revenge  and even that's not 100 real  as it turns out he was part of a  daydream about monster island concocted  by the film's protagonist  a young boy named ichiro a latchkey kid  plagued by a grade school goon he  nicknames  gabara ichiro escapes from reality by  imagining himself on monster island  where he's befriended by godzilla's  offspring minya  the pint-sized kaiju also has to contend  with its own tormentor  similarly named gabra who is a reptilian  amphibian jerk of a monster with the  ability to transmit an electric shock to  his victims  with ichiro's help and some tough love  encouragement from godzilla  minya is able to best gabra which gives  ichiro the strength to take down his own  gabra back in the real world  as godzilla grew in power to a seemingly  indestructible force of nature some of  his on-screen opponents tapped into his  incredible mutated biology in order to  create a means of defeating the creature  as a result several monsters have been  directly spawned from godzilla's  cellular structure  for example there's the colossal plant  monster biolante  in godzilla vs violante the  extraterrestrial clone space godzilla  in godzilla vs space godzilla and orga  a creature formed from dna data stolen  by alien invaders in godzilla 2000  millennium in 